1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:01:00,320
=www.kissasia.co =

2
00:00:02,350 --> 00:00:03,936
[Death Confirmation Report] Now that Cheung Wai Keung is dead,

3
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:05,296
I've got a new assignment for you.

4
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:06,350
Thank you, sir!

5
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:08,246
You're here to poach him already?

6
00:00:08,270 --> 00:00:09,017
Aren't you a bit too eager?

7
00:00:09,041 --> 00:00:11,406
I heard the force's rising star is finally available,

8
00:00:11,430 --> 00:00:12,966
so of course I came straight over to poach him.

9
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:13,750
This is Mok Fei Foon.

10
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:15,646
He's joining the CCB today. [♪CCB: Commercial Crime Bureau]

11
00:00:15,670 --> 00:00:17,230
According to information from Interpol,

12
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:20,040
a transnational counterfeiting syndicate called "Dream weaver"

13
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:21,616
may have arrived

14
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:23,216
in Hong Kong, China over the past year.

15
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:25,536
There are two major sources of counterfeit money in Hong Kong, China.

16
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:27,136
One is the long-established syndicate, Eastern Hall.

17
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:29,216
[Ho Tung Fong] In a previous deal, the other side

18
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:30,646
caught them paying in counterfeit notes.

19
00:00:30,670 --> 00:00:31,486
The second

20
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:32,510
is Sheng Tung's uncle,

21
00:00:32,670 --> 00:00:33,670
To Si Hong.

22
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:35,966
Don't play games with me.

23
00:00:35,990 --> 00:00:37,670
Where did you get those counterfeit notes?

24
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:41,520
You said your counterfeit notes were top-notch.

25
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:42,936
How did anyone know they were fake?

26
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:44,246
No matter how good the quality is,

27
00:00:44,270 --> 00:00:45,296
they're still counterfeit.

28
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:46,486
Use too many at once,

29
00:00:46,510 --> 00:00:47,377
and it's bound to raise suspicion.

30
00:00:47,401 --> 00:00:48,566
Look at my hand.

31
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:50,110
I lost a finger!

32
00:00:50,670 --> 00:00:51,646
I'm warning you,

33
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:52,670
crossing Sheng Tung...

34
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:29,620
♪ With you, it's like I can breathe again ♪

35
00:01:30,050 --> 00:01:32,820
♪ I can't live without this breath, this heartbeat ♪

36
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:35,730
♪ Forever's too far, but you're right here ♪

37
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,160
♪ Together we'll take on this jaded world ♪

38
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:41,140
♪ With you, I'll cross the dark, outrun the pain, and run away ♪

39
00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:45,300
♪ Still believing in true love, no matter how naive, calling you ♪

40
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:50,090
♪ I'm willing to wait ♪

41
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:53,780
♪ I love you like you're a part of me ♪

42
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:56,580
♪ I want to share my life with you ♪

43
00:01:57,220 --> 00:02:03,000
♪ To love this deeply, I'll give a little more ♪

44
00:02:03,350 --> 00:02:05,150
♪ In this cold and gray city ♪

45
00:02:05,230 --> 00:02:06,936
♪ Through all the pain, I'll hold you. Is it true? ♪

46
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:09,310
♪ Pieces of our memories slowly fade ♪

47
00:02:09,390 --> 00:02:09,970
♪ Stay with me ♪

48
00:02:10,110 --> 00:02:12,720
♪ Do you remember the day we crossed paths? ♪

49
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:13,500
♪ Stay with me ♪

50
00:02:13,580 --> 00:02:16,420
♪ Do you remember the forever we promised? ♪

51
00:02:16,910 --> 00:02:18,920
♪ Who's waiting for you to save them? ♪

52
00:02:19,450 --> 00:02:21,960
♪ My heart aches, breaks, and struggles on ♪

53
00:02:22,490 --> 00:02:25,000
♪ How can I hold on to everything in one moment? ♪

54
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:29,220
♪ Stop blaming fate and learn to let it be ♪

55
00:02:31,070 --> 00:02:33,100
[Ash] [Episode 3]

56
00:02:42,510 --> 00:02:43,750
Hey! Cut it out!

57
00:02:45,110 --> 00:02:46,510
Are you crazy?

58
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:53,080
What are you up to now?

59
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:56,200
I'll help you get undressed.

60
00:02:57,350 --> 00:02:58,960
If you keep this up,

61
00:02:59,110 --> 00:03:00,960
I'll report you for trespassing.

62
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:02,160
Come on.

63
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:08,400
Take it off.

64
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:12,800
Sit.

65
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:19,590
Sit. I'll wash your hair.

66
00:03:27,510 --> 00:03:28,670
To,

67
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:30,910
you actually know what you're doing.

68
00:03:34,510 --> 00:03:36,190
When my brother was little,

69
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:38,960
I was always the one who bathed him.

70
00:03:49,190 --> 00:03:50,190
It's healed.

71
00:03:51,350 --> 00:03:52,350
What?

72
00:03:56,750 --> 00:03:57,750
Oh, this?

73
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:00,640
Yeah, got hit by an ashtray.

74
00:04:02,910 --> 00:04:04,240
It's nothing.

75
00:04:04,590 --> 00:04:06,216
My hair usually covers it.

76
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,240
People can't tell.

77
00:04:10,430 --> 00:04:11,430
I'm sorry.

78
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:16,720
Why are you making that face?

79
00:04:18,110 --> 00:04:20,590
I won't let anything like that happen again.

80
00:04:45,190 --> 00:04:46,830
Don't touch the wound.

81
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:48,320
I know.

82
00:04:56,910 --> 00:04:58,640
You're blowing germs into the wound.

83
00:05:01,430 --> 00:05:02,880
Then I'll disinfect it again, okay?

84
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:04,400
Keep it up, and you'll regret it.

85
00:05:27,510 --> 00:05:28,510
All done.

86
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:33,320
If you're done, I'm going to rest.

87
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:36,400
Get up.

88
00:05:36,910 --> 00:05:38,110
Your hair's still wet.

89
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:40,510
It's okay.

90
00:05:41,350 --> 00:05:42,087
No, it's not.

91
00:05:42,111 --> 00:05:43,711
You'll get a headache and catch a chill.

92
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:55,160
Are you still with the Narcotics Bureau?

93
00:05:56,510 --> 00:05:57,960
I've been transferred to the CCB.

94
00:05:59,190 --> 00:06:00,350
Why ask all of a sudden?

95
00:06:01,750 --> 00:06:04,510
Shouldn't it be much safer

96
00:06:04,590 --> 00:06:06,510
in the Commercial Crime Bureau?

97
00:06:06,670 --> 00:06:08,240
How did you get hurt?

98
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:11,696
I was attacked by someone with a knife.

99
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:13,726
I fell dodging him and scraped myself.

100
00:06:13,750 --> 00:06:14,910
It's only a minor injury.

101
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:17,720
Someone with a knife?

102
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:19,430
What do you mean?

103
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:20,960
Were you in danger?

104
00:06:22,510 --> 00:06:23,696
Calm down.

105
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:24,880
We're tracking him down.

106
00:06:25,270 --> 00:06:26,880
We'll find him soon.

107
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:28,800
How do you expect me to calm down?

108
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:32,360
Am I supposed to wait until something happens to you and then regret it?

109
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:36,640
Why do you suddenly care so much about me?

110
00:06:39,990 --> 00:06:41,880
You don't know how to look after yourself.

111
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:43,830
Find another job.

112
00:06:44,270 --> 00:06:45,270
Find another job?

113
00:06:45,350 --> 00:06:46,350
What job?

114
00:06:46,590 --> 00:06:47,856
Anything.

115
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:49,430
Just stop being a police officer.

116
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:53,110
You can be head of security at my company.

117
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:54,966
Or you can

118
00:06:54,990 --> 00:06:55,990
just retire.

119
00:06:57,080 --> 00:06:58,080
Retire?

120
00:06:58,320 --> 00:06:59,480
Are you going to support me?

121
00:06:59,670 --> 00:07:00,670
Sure.

122
00:07:00,750 --> 00:07:01,880
I can afford it.

123
00:07:02,430 --> 00:07:03,240
Right.

124
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:04,456
I almost forgot.

125
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:06,520
You're the business world's most eligible bachelor.

126
00:07:07,830 --> 00:07:09,400
I'm just a regular cop.

127
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:11,720
I wouldn't cost you much.

128
00:07:13,750 --> 00:07:15,350
Then I'll take that as a yes.

129
00:07:15,430 --> 00:07:18,480
Hand in your resignation first thing tomorrow.

130
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:19,457
You're ridiculous.

131
00:07:19,481 --> 00:07:20,510
Who said I agreed?

132
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:32,560
How about this?

133
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:35,910
I made you mad before,

134
00:07:36,270 --> 00:07:37,510
and now you've made me mad.

135
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:39,670
Let's call it even, okay?

136
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,960
No more fighting from now on, okay?

137
00:07:59,320 --> 00:08:00,480
Lucky you.

138
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:02,720
I'm generous enough to let it slide.

139
00:08:03,430 --> 00:08:05,080
You don't get many chances like this.

140
00:08:06,350 --> 00:08:08,350
So behave yourself from now on. Got it?

141
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:09,990
Same goes for you.

142
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:11,320
Me? What about me?

143
00:08:12,510 --> 00:08:14,350
I'm the only one you can have.

144
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:18,190
I'll think about it.

145
00:08:24,510 --> 00:08:25,510
Where are you going?

146
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:27,160
To get the hairdryer.

147
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:29,640
Why?

148
00:08:29,750 --> 00:08:30,830
Do you want me to stay?

149
00:08:31,830 --> 00:08:32,830
Yes.

150
00:08:51,990 --> 00:08:52,990
Forget it.

151
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:55,430
So we'll just sleep?

152
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:02,800
Okay.

153
00:11:54,320 --> 00:11:55,320
Morning.

154
00:11:55,990 --> 00:11:56,990
You're up?

155
00:11:57,830 --> 00:11:58,830
What are you making?

156
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:02,640
An all-day breakfast just for you.

157
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:05,830
Sausages, toast and fried eggs.

158
00:12:06,750 --> 00:12:09,510
And I just went out for cherry tomatoes and lettuce.

159
00:12:12,510 --> 00:12:14,856
So you just cook everything in the pan,

160
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:18,160
then take it out and plate it up?

161
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:19,750
Are you eating it or not?

162
00:12:19,990 --> 00:12:21,830
Of course.

163
00:12:22,990 --> 00:12:24,720
I'll eat anything you make.

164
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:29,560
It's just that the sesame dressing has expired.

165
00:12:29,880 --> 00:12:30,880
Do you mind?

166
00:12:31,430 --> 00:12:32,430
Let me see.

167
00:12:34,110 --> 00:12:36,040
It's fine as long as it hasn't gone bad.

168
00:12:39,430 --> 00:12:40,510
Does your wound still hurt?

169
00:12:43,350 --> 00:12:44,217
It's okay.

170
00:12:44,241 --> 00:12:45,430
Still hurts a little.

171
00:12:50,750 --> 00:12:51,560
Let me do it.

172
00:12:51,670 --> 00:12:53,080
No. You'll ruin it.

173
00:12:54,910 --> 00:12:56,160
Are you hungry?

174
00:12:57,190 --> 00:12:58,830
Have some fruit first.

175
00:13:20,910 --> 00:13:22,910
What time are you going back to the station today?

176
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:26,886
My boss wants me checked for any bone injuries.

177
00:13:26,910 --> 00:13:28,510
I've got an appointment this afternoon.

178
00:13:28,910 --> 00:13:31,960
So we can do whatever you want till then.

179
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:35,320
Whatever I want?

180
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:36,480
Mm-hmm.

181
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:15,480
Come here.

182
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:18,800
What are you up to?

183
00:14:23,190 --> 00:14:24,190
What do you think?

184
00:14:59,670 --> 00:15:00,670
Oh...

185
00:15:02,110 --> 00:15:04,080
All that effort, wasted.

186
00:15:04,430 --> 00:15:05,480
It's all your fault.

187
00:15:05,750 --> 00:15:08,480
All you think about is making out.

188
00:15:17,850 --> 00:15:19,410
It's burnt, and you're still eating it?

189
00:15:19,660 --> 00:15:21,260
It's bad for you.

190
00:15:23,930 --> 00:15:25,370
Well, you made it.

191
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:34,470
I told you.

192
00:15:39,390 --> 00:15:40,710
Your assistant's calling.

193
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:41,920
Hello?

194
00:15:42,110 --> 00:15:43,110
Where are you now?

195
00:15:43,230 --> 00:15:44,550
Do you have other meetings today?

196
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:48,160
Hello, it's me.

197
00:15:48,870 --> 00:15:50,550
Who was that?

198
00:15:54,230 --> 00:15:55,230
What do you need?

199
00:15:55,790 --> 00:15:57,950
You have a meeting with a government department later.

200
00:15:58,470 --> 00:15:59,920
You should get going soon.

201
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:01,840
Where are you now?

202
00:16:02,230 --> 00:16:03,256
I'm...

203
00:16:03,280 --> 00:16:04,280
In Yuen Long.

204
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,526
Okay. Please make yourself presentable before you head out.

205
00:16:10,550 --> 00:16:12,600
I'll send you the address after I hang up.

206
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:18,470
Did you do that on purpose?

207
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:19,840
What?

208
00:16:20,390 --> 00:16:21,520
Can't I tease you?

209
00:16:22,630 --> 00:16:24,550
Hey, stop.

210
00:16:26,380 --> 00:16:28,460
[Sham Shuh Po Police Station]

211
00:16:40,310 --> 00:16:41,310
Officer Mok,

212
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:43,200
what's got you so happy?

213
00:16:44,550 --> 00:16:45,630
Mind your own business.

214
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:48,390
Any leads on that motorbike I asked you to check?

215
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:49,680
I checked.

216
00:16:49,920 --> 00:16:50,960
The number plate was fake.

217
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:52,846
None of the CCTV cameras on the nearby streets

218
00:16:52,870 --> 00:16:54,000
caught him.

219
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:56,200
But I have a theory.

220
00:16:57,390 --> 00:16:58,256
Look at you, taking initiative.

221
00:16:58,280 --> 00:16:59,280
Let's hear it.

222
00:17:00,550 --> 00:17:03,310
I think the casino owner was trying to have us killed.

223
00:17:04,870 --> 00:17:05,870
Go on.

224
00:17:06,080 --> 00:17:07,080
Think about it.

225
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:09,136
If the casino owner hadn't wanted us dead

226
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:10,310
to keep his secret,

227
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:13,630
why would someone on a motorbike have attacked us with a knife

228
00:17:13,790 --> 00:17:15,840
right when To Si Hong was leaving the casino?

229
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:17,760
They must've known we were tailing him.

230
00:17:18,110 --> 00:17:20,576
As soon as we started investigating the casino, they made their move.

231
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:23,790
They must've been afraid we'd uncover their link to the counterfeit money case.

232
00:17:24,310 --> 00:17:25,310
I don't think so.

233
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:26,440
Why not?

234
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:28,280
Think it through.

235
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:33,520
If the casino owner had wanted to protect To Si Hong,

236
00:17:33,630 --> 00:17:36,310
he wouldn't have let To Si Hong show his face before making a move.

237
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:38,896
And he definitely wouldn't have launched an attack on his own turf.

238
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:40,520
That would've been asking to get caught.

239
00:17:40,630 --> 00:17:41,950
That's not how they operate.

240
00:17:43,390 --> 00:17:45,686
Maybe they were just trying to scare us off the investigation.

241
00:17:45,710 --> 00:17:48,230
But that man came straight at us with a knife.

242
00:17:48,310 --> 00:17:49,896
He attacked without hesitation.

243
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:51,280
He was out to kill us.

244
00:17:51,870 --> 00:17:52,737
So I don't think

245
00:17:52,761 --> 00:17:55,200
it was just someone the casino owner hired to scare us.

246
00:17:55,630 --> 00:17:56,630
Really?

247
00:17:57,600 --> 00:17:59,766
I've got more experience with cases like this than you.

248
00:17:59,790 --> 00:18:00,790
Trust me.

249
00:18:01,630 --> 00:18:04,006
But we got attacked as soon as we started investigating the casino.

250
00:18:04,030 --> 00:18:05,230
What are the odds?

251
00:18:05,280 --> 00:18:08,136
I still think the casino is involved.

252
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:09,000
Fair point.

253
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:11,760
But being involved doesn't mean they were behind the attack.

254
00:18:12,550 --> 00:18:14,550
Sir, that's too deep for me.

255
00:18:15,310 --> 00:18:16,366
By your logic,

256
00:18:16,390 --> 00:18:18,000
what leads do we have left to follow?

257
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:19,137
Want to learn?

258
00:18:19,161 --> 00:18:20,446
Make me tea and call me Master first.

259
00:18:20,470 --> 00:18:21,470
What?

260
00:18:26,080 --> 00:18:27,870
I was kidding. Come with me.

261
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:28,920
Okay.

262
00:18:29,860 --> 00:18:32,860
[Tin Ping Group Sales Department]

263
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:35,390
We still can't find Uncle To.

264
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:37,576
I went to his home and office,

265
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:38,920
but I found nothing.

266
00:18:39,550 --> 00:18:41,790
Do we know who Uncle To has been in contact with lately?

267
00:18:42,090 --> 00:18:43,360
I asked Auntie Fan.

268
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:44,510
She hasn't seen

269
00:18:44,590 --> 00:18:46,960
anyone suspicious around him.

270
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:51,950
So nothing on anyone he might be working with?

271
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:54,080
No.

272
00:18:54,950 --> 00:18:56,790
Luk King, stay out of this.

273
00:18:57,030 --> 00:18:59,030
Leave the investigation entirely to Tam Fung.

274
00:18:59,710 --> 00:19:01,440
Is your stomach acting up?

275
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:05,310
Do you need me to take you to hospital?

276
00:19:07,870 --> 00:19:09,470
No. There's no time.

277
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:18,440
Feros has been

278
00:19:18,550 --> 00:19:20,000
competing with us for some time

279
00:19:20,310 --> 00:19:22,710
and has worked with others to take several projects from us.

280
00:19:22,950 --> 00:19:25,110
A lot of our business partners have gone over to them.

281
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:28,200
To put it nicely, they're waiting to see how things play out.

282
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:30,520
To put it harshly, they're waiting for us to lose.

283
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:36,280
Make sure everything is properly arranged for the ceremony later.

284
00:19:36,470 --> 00:19:37,870
There can't be any mistakes.

285
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:41,390
Loek To, don't worry too much.

286
00:19:41,870 --> 00:19:44,256
Feros only entered the Hong Kong, China market and went public last year,

287
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:45,366
yet they've been poaching staff and snapping up projects,

288
00:19:45,390 --> 00:19:46,686
expanding with almost no regard for cost.

289
00:19:46,710 --> 00:19:48,630
I don't think they can keep it up for long.

290
00:19:49,310 --> 00:19:51,030
Even if they can't,

291
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:52,177
I can't just sit back

292
00:19:52,201 --> 00:19:54,870
while they keep poaching our business partners.

293
00:19:56,310 --> 00:19:57,310
Luk King, you know,

294
00:19:58,280 --> 00:20:00,160
capital, time, and corporate reputation

295
00:20:00,440 --> 00:20:02,080
are all intangible costs to the company.

296
00:20:04,760 --> 00:20:06,736
I looked into their corporate background.

297
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:08,680
Feros's parent company is in the UK

298
00:20:08,950 --> 00:20:11,000
and works closely with numerous overseas investors.

299
00:20:11,630 --> 00:20:12,816
Its CEO,

300
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:14,880
who returned from the UK, is from Hong Kong, China.

301
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:16,950
But I couldn't find much about him.

302
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:19,286
I remember his surname is Siu, though.

303
00:20:19,310 --> 00:20:20,280
Does that ring a bell?

304
00:20:20,310 --> 00:20:21,310
No.

305
00:20:21,950 --> 00:20:23,680
There are so many people out there.

306
00:20:23,870 --> 00:20:25,280
I can't possibly know them all.

307
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:28,870
We should get going.

308
00:20:29,830 --> 00:20:30,830
Let's go.

309
00:20:30,870 --> 00:20:31,870
Okay.

310
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:41,180
[Tin Ping Group and Ascend Global Estates Limited Signing Ceremony]

311
00:20:55,360 --> 00:20:57,366
Distinguished guests and members of the media,

312
00:20:57,390 --> 00:20:59,446
welcome to Bay Area Metropolis's

313
00:20:59,470 --> 00:21:01,630
phase one partnership signing ceremony.

314
00:21:01,710 --> 00:21:03,816
Bay Area Metropolis is a key development project

315
00:21:03,840 --> 00:21:05,390
for Tin Ping Group.

316
00:21:05,630 --> 00:21:08,206
It is designed to create a new-generation urban hub in Hong Kong, China

317
00:21:08,230 --> 00:21:11,470
that brings together living, community, business, and leisure.

318
00:21:11,710 --> 00:21:13,310
We're delighted to announce

319
00:21:13,470 --> 00:21:15,606
that Ascend Global Estates Limited will be joining us

320
00:21:15,630 --> 00:21:17,446
as our phase one development partner.

321
00:21:17,470 --> 00:21:20,366
Now, let's welcome Chairman Yiu King Leung of Ascend Global Estates Limited

322
00:21:20,390 --> 00:21:22,870
and Chairman Hui Loek To of Tin Ping Group

323
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:25,520
to complete this simple yet formal signing ceremony.

324
00:21:25,630 --> 00:21:26,630
Please welcome them.

325
00:21:35,460 --> 00:21:41,780
[Mr. Hui Loek To, Chairman of Tin Ping Group]

326
00:21:52,440 --> 00:21:53,680
No need to wait.

327
00:21:54,440 --> 00:21:56,200
Chairman Yiu won't be able to make it today.

328
00:21:58,080 --> 00:21:59,110
Hello, everyone.

329
00:21:59,790 --> 00:22:00,790
My surname is Siu.

330
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:02,950
I'm the CEO of Feros Group.

331
00:22:04,080 --> 00:22:05,200
You can call me Shawn.

332
00:22:06,030 --> 00:22:07,030
Feros Group

333
00:22:07,310 --> 00:22:09,496
has just completed its acquisition of Ascend Global Estates,

334
00:22:09,520 --> 00:22:11,470
so I'm attending today's event

335
00:22:13,080 --> 00:22:14,870
in my new capacity as CEO.

336
00:22:21,230 --> 00:22:22,950
You don't mind if I call you Shawn, do you?

337
00:22:23,160 --> 00:22:24,160
Mr. Hui,

338
00:22:24,390 --> 00:22:26,470
you don't mind if I call you Vincent, do you?

339
00:22:27,950 --> 00:22:29,710
New management, new approach.

340
00:22:30,760 --> 00:22:32,656
You've been in Hong Kong, China for less than a year,

341
00:22:32,680 --> 00:22:35,680
yet every move you've made has taken everyone by surprise.

342
00:22:36,870 --> 00:22:38,470
I'll take that as a compliment, Vincent.

343
00:22:39,710 --> 00:22:40,846
I do admire

344
00:22:40,870 --> 00:22:42,870
the way you've run Tin Ping Group all these years.

345
00:22:43,160 --> 00:22:45,286
I look forward to a chance to work together in the future.

346
00:22:45,310 --> 00:22:46,310
Just

347
00:22:46,920 --> 00:22:47,920
not on this project.

348
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:50,390
You mean you're ending this partnership?

349
00:22:50,790 --> 00:22:51,790
That's right.

350
00:22:52,310 --> 00:22:54,360
We've reviewed Tin Ping's financial position.

351
00:22:54,680 --> 00:22:56,286
I doubt you can even handle

352
00:22:56,310 --> 00:22:57,910
a project as big as Bay Area Metropolis.

353
00:22:59,110 --> 00:23:01,110
I won't let Ascend get dragged down.

354
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:04,160
That's fine.

355
00:23:04,710 --> 00:23:06,920
I rarely work with partners I don't know anyway,

356
00:23:07,520 --> 00:23:10,470
especially those who don't understand the local market

357
00:23:10,760 --> 00:23:12,280
yet invest blindly.

358
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:15,000
Ending the partnership between Tin Ping and Ascend

359
00:23:17,310 --> 00:23:18,710
does us more good than harm.

360
00:23:19,280 --> 00:23:20,550
I completely agree.

361
00:23:21,550 --> 00:23:23,440
But frankly, Vincent,

362
00:23:23,870 --> 00:23:25,920
you'd better check Tin Ping's cash flow.

363
00:23:26,710 --> 00:23:27,920
If you find a shortfall

364
00:23:28,110 --> 00:23:30,390
and need to work with Feros,

365
00:23:31,110 --> 00:23:32,110
come talk to me anytime.

366
00:23:33,390 --> 00:23:34,390
Sure.

367
00:23:34,870 --> 00:23:36,160
I'm sure we'll get the chance.

368
00:23:36,360 --> 00:23:37,630
Now, if you'll excuse me.

369
00:23:38,660 --> 00:23:40,660
[Mr. Yiu King Leung]

370
00:23:41,550 --> 00:23:42,550
I have a feeling

371
00:23:44,390 --> 00:23:45,910
we'll be seeing each other again soon.

372
00:23:46,840 --> 00:23:47,840
I look forward to it.

373
00:24:01,160 --> 00:24:02,686
Officer Mok, where exactly are you taking me?

374
00:24:02,710 --> 00:24:03,766
To meet a real expert.

375
00:24:03,790 --> 00:24:04,830
He really knows his stuff.

376
00:24:05,280 --> 00:24:06,007
Who is it?

377
00:24:06,031 --> 00:24:07,080
Why so many questions?

378
00:24:07,110 --> 00:24:08,360
You'll find out soon enough.

379
00:24:08,440 --> 00:24:09,030
Right.

380
00:24:09,110 --> 00:24:10,110
Hey, Fung Gor.

381
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:15,006
You scared me,

382
00:24:15,030 --> 00:24:16,030
Mok Fei Foon.

383
00:24:16,230 --> 00:24:16,976
Long time no see.

384
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:17,817
I thought you were dead.

385
00:24:17,841 --> 00:24:18,926
Don't curse me.

386
00:24:18,950 --> 00:24:20,630
I was going to ask you out for a ride.

387
00:24:21,310 --> 00:24:22,686
You wouldn't come all this way for nothing.

388
00:24:22,710 --> 00:24:23,710
What do you want?

389
00:24:24,200 --> 00:24:25,920
I need to ask you something.

390
00:24:26,230 --> 00:24:28,006
Has any one of your customers brought in

391
00:24:28,030 --> 00:24:29,550
a motorbike for modification recently?

392
00:24:29,710 --> 00:24:32,416
A 2020 Yamaha R1.

393
00:24:32,440 --> 00:24:33,496
Slim build,

394
00:24:33,520 --> 00:24:35,110
about 1.75 metres tall.

395
00:24:36,080 --> 00:24:38,286
I get tons of customers here.

396
00:24:38,310 --> 00:24:39,870
How am I supposed to remember them all?

397
00:24:40,110 --> 00:24:41,656
Maybe you don't remember the person,

398
00:24:41,680 --> 00:24:43,000
but surely you remember the bike.

399
00:24:43,630 --> 00:24:45,176
Pretty much everyone in Hong Kong, China

400
00:24:45,200 --> 00:24:46,336
comes to you for motorbike modifications,

401
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:47,360
right?

402
00:24:48,840 --> 00:24:50,110
Think carefully.

403
00:24:50,870 --> 00:24:54,470
The body and rims were both wrapped in gold and blue,

404
00:24:55,680 --> 00:24:59,110
with a ten-centimetre scratch above the left headlight.

405
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:01,526
It came at us so fast,

406
00:25:01,550 --> 00:25:02,760
and you still saw all that?

407
00:25:03,160 --> 00:25:05,030
Do I have to tell you I've got eagle eyes?

408
00:25:08,230 --> 00:25:09,007
I remember now.

409
00:25:09,031 --> 00:25:10,080
That guy said he'd

410
00:25:10,310 --> 00:25:12,590
just bought the bike and brought it in for modifications.

411
00:25:12,630 --> 00:25:14,680
But I could tell straight away it wasn't legit.

412
00:25:15,160 --> 00:25:17,030
He paid me very well,

413
00:25:17,230 --> 00:25:18,440
so I didn't ask questions.

414
00:25:19,360 --> 00:25:22,200
Do you remember anything distinctive about his appearance?

415
00:25:23,310 --> 00:25:24,310
Distinctive?

416
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:29,230
He had a lightning-bolt tattoo on the back of his neck.

417
00:25:30,630 --> 00:25:33,280
I also heard him refer to himself

418
00:25:35,280 --> 00:25:36,280
as K on the phone.

419
00:25:51,870 --> 00:25:52,870
Yee Gor, don't worry.

420
00:25:54,030 --> 00:25:55,440
I'll take care of him

421
00:25:56,280 --> 00:25:57,280
and avenge you.

422
00:26:01,680 --> 00:26:04,256
So the knife man at the casino was after you.

423
00:26:04,280 --> 00:26:06,110
Officer Mok, what are you going to do?

424
00:26:06,470 --> 00:26:08,136
I'll report it to my superior.

425
00:26:08,160 --> 00:26:09,280
Don't worry about it.

426
00:26:13,260 --> 00:26:16,060
[Hui Loek To: Are you done with work? Where should I pick you up?]

427
00:26:16,310 --> 00:26:16,847
All right.

428
00:26:16,871 --> 00:26:17,926
It's quitting time.

429
00:26:17,950 --> 00:26:18,990
Go home and get some rest.

430
00:26:19,390 --> 00:26:20,390
Sir,

431
00:26:20,710 --> 00:26:22,686
didn't you say we'd leave after finishing what we were working on?

432
00:26:22,710 --> 00:26:24,470
We just found a new lead.

433
00:26:25,230 --> 00:26:26,630
You want to work overtime?

434
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:28,030
Perfect.

435
00:26:28,390 --> 00:26:30,080
Go check the stolen-vehicle records.

436
00:26:30,360 --> 00:26:31,840
You know how to do that, right?

437
00:26:33,230 --> 00:26:33,896
Bye-bye.

438
00:26:33,920 --> 00:26:34,390
But...

439
00:26:34,840 --> 00:26:35,687
Get to it.

440
00:26:35,711 --> 00:26:37,231
Don't hold me up. I'm meeting someone.

441
00:26:39,520 --> 00:26:40,520
Yes, sir.

442
00:26:41,180 --> 00:26:44,916
♪ Let the world judge all it wants ♪

443
00:26:44,940 --> 00:26:48,596
♪ All I want is that when we meet, I can smile ♪

444
00:26:48,620 --> 00:26:52,396
♪ And say, "I'm so glad it's you" ♪

445
00:26:52,420 --> 00:26:55,956
♪ The time is right, even the wind is on our side ♪

446
00:26:55,980 --> 00:26:59,316
♪ At this very moment, the sun and moon shine on us ♪

447
00:26:59,340 --> 00:27:01,316
♪ Never mind what others may say ♪

448
00:27:01,340 --> 00:27:02,916
♪ Never mind how wild the rumours run ♪

449
00:27:02,940 --> 00:27:06,036
♪ I just happened to meet you, and that's all that matters ♪

450
00:27:06,060 --> 00:27:09,220
♪ The time is right, true love is on our side ♪

451
00:27:09,880 --> 00:27:10,880
Knock it off.

452
00:27:12,590 --> 00:27:13,800
Just cooling you down.

453
00:27:14,700 --> 00:27:16,436
♪ No need to pretend we're distant ♪

454
00:27:16,460 --> 00:27:19,726
♪ I just happened to meet you, and that's all that matters ♪

455
00:27:19,750 --> 00:27:20,750
Thanks.

456
00:27:26,510 --> 00:27:29,160
How's the investigation into the knife attack going?

457
00:27:29,720 --> 00:27:31,120
We've pretty much figured it out.

458
00:27:31,880 --> 00:27:33,270
We know who he is now.

459
00:27:33,990 --> 00:27:36,640
He was one of my old boss's men when I was working undercover.

460
00:27:39,510 --> 00:27:40,910
He wants to avenge his boss.

461
00:27:41,400 --> 00:27:42,910
We're tracking him down now.

462
00:27:43,480 --> 00:27:44,480
Good.

463
00:27:44,960 --> 00:27:46,430
When you arrest him,

464
00:27:46,510 --> 00:27:48,270
make sure Officer Lam goes in first.

465
00:27:48,400 --> 00:27:49,560
He can take the hit for you.

466
00:27:49,990 --> 00:27:51,456
Don't joke about things like that.

467
00:27:51,480 --> 00:27:52,480
It's bad luck.

468
00:27:52,880 --> 00:27:53,880
Everything's fine

469
00:27:53,960 --> 00:27:54,960
until you say it.

470
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:56,680
Are you saying someone might get hurt?

471
00:27:58,560 --> 00:27:59,560
It'll be fine.

472
00:28:00,320 --> 00:28:01,400
Don't worry.

473
00:28:04,510 --> 00:28:06,120
Doesn't sound like it'll be fine.

474
00:28:09,400 --> 00:28:10,480
Once we arrest him,

475
00:28:11,270 --> 00:28:14,270
my undercover assignment as Cheung Wai Keung will officially be over.

476
00:28:15,270 --> 00:28:17,670
Are you sure he doesn't have any other accomplices?

477
00:28:18,640 --> 00:28:19,640
What if he does?

478
00:28:19,670 --> 00:28:20,670
Then what?

479
00:28:23,590 --> 00:28:25,750
Since when do you know so much about gang business?

480
00:28:29,320 --> 00:28:30,856
Have you been

481
00:28:30,880 --> 00:28:32,486
doing all sorts of shady things

482
00:28:32,510 --> 00:28:33,566
and never telling me?

483
00:28:33,590 --> 00:28:35,190
It's just common sense.

484
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:38,696
Gangsters rarely go alone on dangerous jobs.

485
00:28:38,720 --> 00:28:41,510
They usually move in groups of three or five.

486
00:28:41,720 --> 00:28:44,880
I'm a police officer. Situations like this come with the job.

487
00:28:44,910 --> 00:28:45,857
Even if it's dangerous,

488
00:28:45,881 --> 00:28:46,921
I still have to do my job.

489
00:28:52,480 --> 00:28:55,270
Why not come off the front line?

490
00:29:01,560 --> 00:29:02,560
What?

491
00:29:03,040 --> 00:29:05,200
You want me to back off whenever things get dangerous?

492
00:29:05,590 --> 00:29:08,510
Do you think I'm the type to run away?

493
00:29:08,720 --> 00:29:10,720
No, and that's exactly why I'm telling you this.

494
00:29:12,830 --> 00:29:15,070
I really don't think you should stay on front line duty.

495
00:29:15,480 --> 00:29:16,510
Take a desk job.

496
00:29:17,070 --> 00:29:18,670
You can still do plenty of good there.

497
00:29:19,720 --> 00:29:21,910
You'd have a safe office with air conditioning,

498
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:23,160
a clear career path,

499
00:29:23,480 --> 00:29:24,720
and no need to risk your life.

500
00:29:26,720 --> 00:29:28,120
It is safe.

501
00:29:28,670 --> 00:29:29,830
But it's not what I want.

502
00:29:31,320 --> 00:29:32,670
So being out in all weathers

503
00:29:33,070 --> 00:29:34,670
and risking your life is what you want?

504
00:29:37,800 --> 00:29:38,800
I'm not being stubborn.

505
00:29:39,800 --> 00:29:42,510
This is my choice.

506
00:29:43,990 --> 00:29:45,400
No matter how hard it gets,

507
00:29:45,640 --> 00:29:47,400
no matter what it costs me,

508
00:29:47,990 --> 00:29:50,640
I want to bring criminals to justice

509
00:29:51,910 --> 00:29:53,640
and help people in need.

510
00:29:54,320 --> 00:29:55,320
That's the reason.

511
00:29:56,590 --> 00:29:58,390
I became a police officer in the first place.

512
00:30:07,800 --> 00:30:08,880
You didn't bring a lighter?

513
00:30:09,120 --> 00:30:10,120
No.

514
00:30:24,510 --> 00:30:25,510
I get it.

515
00:30:27,590 --> 00:30:28,870
But I just can't agree with you.

516
00:30:34,590 --> 00:30:36,990
If you overthink everything,

517
00:30:37,310 --> 00:30:39,150
you'll only end up lost and unsure.

518
00:30:43,050 --> 00:30:44,210
Do you remember

519
00:30:44,290 --> 00:30:46,880
the first film we ever watched together?

520
00:30:47,510 --> 00:30:48,990
Of course I do.

521
00:30:49,040 --> 00:30:51,400
You made me watch a romantic film for no reason.

522
00:30:51,510 --> 00:30:52,720
A romantic film?

523
00:30:52,830 --> 00:30:53,990
Which one was it?

524
00:30:55,040 --> 00:30:56,406
That one.

525
00:30:56,430 --> 00:30:57,377
I remember.

526
00:30:57,401 --> 00:30:58,750
Leon Lai was in it.

527
00:30:58,880 --> 00:31:00,230
Who was the female lead?

528
00:31:00,360 --> 00:31:01,720
The female lead?

529
00:31:14,200 --> 00:31:16,200
Lai Siu Kwan and Lee Kiu

530
00:31:16,830 --> 00:31:18,720
spent all those years going round in circles.

531
00:31:19,510 --> 00:31:21,230
They clearly loved each other deeply,

532
00:31:22,480 --> 00:31:25,120
but reality kept holding them back,

533
00:31:25,990 --> 00:31:27,990
so they missed their chance time and again.

534
00:31:29,150 --> 00:31:30,150
Any thoughts?

535
00:31:30,510 --> 00:31:32,880
If they'd been truer to what they really wanted

536
00:31:33,280 --> 00:31:34,430
and worried less,

537
00:31:34,640 --> 00:31:37,400
would things have ended with fewer regrets?

538
00:31:38,120 --> 00:31:40,640
I don't think the problem was that they worried too much.

539
00:31:42,120 --> 00:31:44,070
It was that Lai Siu Kwan and Lee Kiu

540
00:31:44,200 --> 00:31:46,670
always thought there'd be another chance,

541
00:31:47,200 --> 00:31:48,760
that their feelings would never change.

542
00:31:49,510 --> 00:31:50,910
But they never considered

543
00:31:51,880 --> 00:31:53,096
that life changes,

544
00:31:53,120 --> 00:31:54,360
the world changes,

545
00:31:54,590 --> 00:31:56,640
and most of all, time passes.

546
00:31:58,910 --> 00:32:01,270
Sometimes, if you miss your chance with someone, that's it.

547
00:32:03,420 --> 00:32:04,790
The ending

548
00:32:04,870 --> 00:32:07,180
was only there so the audience

549
00:32:07,880 --> 00:32:09,240
wouldn't be left with any regrets.

550
00:32:09,550 --> 00:32:10,790
It doesn't really mean much.

551
00:32:12,500 --> 00:32:13,850
Then I disagree.

552
00:32:17,020 --> 00:32:18,830
What makes their relationship so moving

553
00:32:19,330 --> 00:32:21,890
is that they couldn't help loving each other despite everything.

554
00:32:23,080 --> 00:32:27,270
Most people are pushed along by circumstances.

555
00:32:27,730 --> 00:32:28,730
Not everyone is like you,

556
00:32:28,930 --> 00:32:30,730
able to keep everything firmly under control.

557
00:32:33,470 --> 00:32:35,030
But the way they cared about each other

558
00:32:35,100 --> 00:32:36,516
and the feelings they had for each other

559
00:32:36,540 --> 00:32:37,890
never changed

560
00:32:39,210 --> 00:32:40,260
from beginning to end.

561
00:32:42,540 --> 00:32:45,180
And I think a love that pure

562
00:32:45,930 --> 00:32:49,090
is far more precious than having no regrets.

563
00:32:50,210 --> 00:32:51,306
No matter how precious it is,

564
00:32:51,330 --> 00:32:53,540
nothing matters more than staying alive.

565
00:32:55,100 --> 00:32:57,940
I don't think anyone wants to miss their chance with the one they love.

566
00:32:59,300 --> 00:33:00,890
If you're not even alive anymore,

567
00:33:01,570 --> 00:33:02,916
no matter how deep the attachment

568
00:33:02,940 --> 00:33:04,330
or how sincere the feelings,

569
00:33:04,860 --> 00:33:05,900
it'll all come to nothing.

570
00:33:06,490 --> 00:33:08,210
Just think about that Mickey Mouse.

571
00:33:09,060 --> 00:33:11,700
But if you've got something like that Mickey Mouse tattoo

572
00:33:11,780 --> 00:33:13,580
that can make the one you love laugh and cry,

573
00:33:14,750 --> 00:33:16,430
then you've lived a life worth living.

574
00:33:29,170 --> 00:33:30,730
That's why I say you've got no taste.

575
00:33:31,860 --> 00:33:33,946
That film portrays its characters' inner lives so delicately

576
00:33:33,970 --> 00:33:36,436
and weaves the period setting so skilfully

577
00:33:36,460 --> 00:33:38,300
into the characters' fates,

578
00:33:39,620 --> 00:33:41,100
and you say I forced you to watch it.

579
00:33:42,830 --> 00:33:45,710
[Private Property, No Entry]

580
00:33:57,810 --> 00:33:58,810
What are you doing?

581
00:33:59,300 --> 00:34:01,300
Trying to carve another Mickey Mouse?

582
00:34:02,330 --> 00:34:03,330
What is it, Officer?

583
00:34:03,460 --> 00:34:04,820
Going to charge me with vandalism?

584
00:34:05,100 --> 00:34:06,660
It depends on how good your drawing is.

585
00:34:12,730 --> 00:34:13,730
What is this?

586
00:34:14,130 --> 00:34:15,130
Our cigarette.

587
00:34:17,890 --> 00:34:18,890
Seriously, Mr. Hui?

588
00:34:19,730 --> 00:34:21,700
Your drawing skills need work.

589
00:34:22,700 --> 00:34:24,050
Give it to me.

590
00:34:54,240 --> 00:34:55,240
Much better.

591
00:35:05,410 --> 00:35:06,410
Hello?

592
00:35:09,540 --> 00:35:10,780
All right. I'm coming back now.

593
00:35:10,810 --> 00:35:12,100
Copy that. I'll be right there.

594
00:35:14,130 --> 00:35:16,026
- I've got a case to deal with.
- Something's come up at the office.

595
00:35:16,050 --> 00:35:17,050
Let's go.

596
00:35:18,380 --> 00:35:19,380
Get in.

597
00:35:24,970 --> 00:35:26,410
What you've been dealing with lately

598
00:35:26,650 --> 00:35:27,810
isn't against the law, is it?

599
00:35:29,130 --> 00:35:30,856
Someone was being ungrateful.

600
00:35:30,880 --> 00:35:32,120
I just taught him a lesson.

601
00:35:33,260 --> 00:35:35,210
That's not illegal, is it, Officer?

602
00:35:36,130 --> 00:35:37,860
Just be careful.

603
00:35:39,370 --> 00:35:40,770
I should be saying that to you.

604
00:35:40,880 --> 00:35:42,160
Be careful.

605
00:35:55,650 --> 00:35:58,250
[Harbour Crystal Centre]

606
00:36:02,890 --> 00:36:03,700
Auntie Fan.

607
00:36:03,860 --> 00:36:05,100
Vincent.

608
00:36:05,130 --> 00:36:06,516
Why? Why did you do this?

609
00:36:06,540 --> 00:36:07,916
- Auntie Fan, calm down.
- Why? Why did you do this?

610
00:36:07,940 --> 00:36:08,707
Calm down?

611
00:36:08,731 --> 00:36:10,940
You need to explain this to me!

612
00:36:12,330 --> 00:36:13,730
The police found Uncle To's body.

613
00:36:14,100 --> 00:36:14,890
What happened?

614
00:36:15,020 --> 00:36:16,180
I need some time to find out.

615
00:36:16,730 --> 00:36:17,866
He was perfectly fine.

616
00:36:17,890 --> 00:36:19,546
After he came to see you here, he was killed.

617
00:36:19,570 --> 00:36:20,970
Tell me what happened.

618
00:36:21,300 --> 00:36:23,546
Auntie Fan, Uncle To did come to me.

619
00:36:23,570 --> 00:36:24,547
But I swear,

620
00:36:24,571 --> 00:36:26,130
I had nothing to do with his death.

621
00:36:26,260 --> 00:36:27,260
Then why?

622
00:36:27,780 --> 00:36:29,260
Why did he die so miserably?

623
00:36:30,020 --> 00:36:32,570
Auntie Fan, calm down and think carefully.

624
00:36:32,860 --> 00:36:34,676
Who had Uncle To been seeing lately?

625
00:36:34,700 --> 00:36:37,050
Where had he been, and who had he contacted?

626
00:36:42,630 --> 00:36:43,990
[Police]

627
00:36:44,050 --> 00:36:45,330
Hong Kong, China Police!

628
00:36:45,540 --> 00:36:46,700
Everyone inside, listen up.

629
00:36:46,860 --> 00:36:49,340
We suspect someone on the premises is using counterfeit notes.

630
00:36:49,540 --> 00:36:51,546
We have a court-issued search warrant.

631
00:36:51,570 --> 00:36:52,700
Open the door immediately.

632
00:36:53,180 --> 00:36:54,706
Do not obstruct us in the course of our duties.

633
00:36:54,730 --> 00:36:56,490
If you refuse, we will force entry.

634
00:36:57,650 --> 00:36:58,650
Open the door!

635
00:37:00,730 --> 00:37:01,437
Boss,

636
00:37:01,461 --> 00:37:02,650
the police are outside.

637
00:37:06,670 --> 00:37:08,400
Auntie Fan, about Uncle To,

638
00:37:08,430 --> 00:37:10,020
we'll talk later. Wait here for me.

639
00:37:13,330 --> 00:37:15,276
Remember, as far as the public knows, you're the chairman of Tin Ping.

640
00:37:15,300 --> 00:37:17,970
If this blows up and Mrs. Hui hears about it, we're in trouble.

641
00:37:18,100 --> 00:37:19,100
Got it.

642
00:37:22,810 --> 00:37:23,517
Turn on the lights.

643
00:37:23,541 --> 00:37:24,650
Routine police check.

644
00:37:25,180 --> 00:37:26,740
Everyone, get up and stand to the side.

645
00:37:27,020 --> 00:37:28,210
Show your IDs.

646
00:37:28,700 --> 00:37:29,730
Move it.

647
00:37:32,890 --> 00:37:33,890
Officers,

648
00:37:34,620 --> 00:37:35,940
how can I assist you?

649
00:37:36,590 --> 00:37:38,150
We're with the Commercial Crime Bureau.

650
00:37:38,840 --> 00:37:39,840
Are you in charge here?

651
00:37:40,310 --> 00:37:41,310
I am.

652
00:37:41,860 --> 00:37:42,900
Here's the search warrant.

653
00:37:43,380 --> 00:37:45,436
We suspect someone here of using and possessing

654
00:37:45,460 --> 00:37:46,700
counterfeit notes.

655
00:37:47,490 --> 00:37:48,100
Go.

656
00:37:48,200 --> 00:37:49,200
Take him in.

657
00:37:51,680 --> 00:37:52,440
Mr. Hui,

658
00:37:52,680 --> 00:37:55,400
please come with us to the station to assist with our investigation.

659
00:37:55,790 --> 00:37:57,280
Need a hood?

660
00:37:58,080 --> 00:37:59,200
This is my turf.

661
00:37:59,680 --> 00:38:00,950
I've got nothing to fear.

662
00:38:04,230 --> 00:38:05,230
Look out!

663
00:38:06,950 --> 00:38:08,200
You traitor!

664
00:38:21,440 --> 00:38:22,840
Joseph, call an ambulance.

665
00:38:23,030 --> 00:38:24,030
Yes, sir.

666
00:38:24,680 --> 00:38:26,790
Shots fired. Someone's been hit. Send an ambulance.

667
00:38:33,530 --> 00:38:34,530
Are you all right?

668
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:38,400
Take everyone back to the station. We'll deal with it there!

669
00:38:42,360 --> 00:38:43,680
Come back to the station with me.

670
00:38:51,660 --> 00:38:56,700
[Episode 3]

671
00:38:56,790 --> 00:39:04,790
[This story is fictional. Any resemblance is entirely coincidental.]
